{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqqosxptv7i","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"stale reaper readiness root cause is done only dependency gate","summary":"Root cause of judge staying not_ready after a tested impl: in daemon.js makeResolver().effective (line ~1965) a dependent readies only when every blocking dep resolves to === 'done'. A worker completing with status 'tested' (the required impl terminal status, NOT done) sets ov.status[key]='tested' which effective() returns verbatim, so the blocked_by judge never readies and newly_ready (readyBefore vs readyAfter diff in routes/overlay.js) comes up empty. This fires INDEPENDENT of the stale-claim reap: the reap (10min default in daemon.js staleClaimKeys) only deletes the in_progress override, but once the late completion writes 'tested' the dep gate still rejects it. Fix is to treat terminal-success statuses (done AND tested) as dependency-satisfying. Reaper mitigation: align claim-sweep default to the 1h git lease (LEASE_STALE_MS) and don't reap a worktree-backed claim whose attempt branch has fresh commits.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T13:35:32.273Z","vec":[-0.07333820313215256,-0.03874373435974121,0.02344270795583725,0.01129824947565794,0.05519949272274971,-0.0995463877916336,-0.06898847222328186,-0.018028495833277702,0.041154537349939346,0.10009616613388062,0.053706057369709015,0.008200124837458134,-0.04452227056026459,0.0034963395446538925,0.014139583334326744,0.029628973454236984,0.0768197625875473,-0.03421466052532196,-0.02154923602938652,-0.04791799932718277,-0.03455213084816933,0.03447185084223747,0.006293168291449547,0.0353686586022377,-0.046393707394599915,-0.05711618810892105,-0.09814728051424026,-0.009076598100364208,0.038429033011198044,-0.03125252202153206,-0.008364290930330753,0.06732221692800522,-0.10244700312614441,-0.04779905825853348,0.013913564383983612,0.1223696917295456,-0.001524344552308321,-0.013900615274906158,-0.04956357926130295,0.01145165320485