{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqqosxptv7i","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"Root cause of judge staying not_ready after a tested impl: in daemon.js makeResolver().effective (line ~1965) a dependent readies only when every blocking dep resolves to === 'done'. A worker completing with status 'tested' (the required impl terminal status, NOT done) sets ov.status[key]='tested' which effective() returns verbatim, so the blocked_by judge never readies and newly_ready (readyBefore vs readyAfter diff in routes/overlay.js) comes up empty. This fires INDEPENDENT of the stale-claim reap: the reap (10min default in daemon.js staleClaimKeys) only deletes the in_progress override, but once the late completion writes 'tested' the dep gate still rejects it. Fix is to treat terminal-success statuses (done AND tested) as dependency-satisfying. Reaper mitigation: align claim-sweep default to the 1h git lease (LEASE_STALE_MS) and don't reap a worktree-backed claim whose attempt branch has fresh commits.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T14:17:45.416Z"}
